-# TASK-260830-1x524u — Shared Runtime Story landing-readiness revalidation
-
-## Verdict
-
-Ready for independent review. The exact Shared Runtime Story candidate passes the configured landing suite and all focused gates. This tester changed no product/runtime source and did not activate a VPN, provider, route, or DNS configuration. The role handoff is expected to publish the required `story_final` Change Request; integration remains orchestrator-owned.
-
-## Candidate integrity and dependency terminality
-
-- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260715-1y04r0` at `9bf4d0892db03035b989a4c040cfee37636ff8df`; freshly fetched remote Story ref matches exactly (`0/0`).
-- Base: `origin/main` and merge-base both `b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74`; Story branch is five commits ahead and zero behind.
-- All five Story commits report Git signature state `G`. Candidate tree before handoff: `d3c3fd9b443a69cb20b6234c97dfaee1c0b7fc48`.
-- All eleven prior direct Story children are `done`; this task is the only active child. Direct blockers `STORY-260715-jnpbyz` (packet bridge/HEV), `STORY-260715-lkshfz` (SSH engine), and `TASK-260715-nphtib` (generated macOS architecture verification) are `done`; Story and task both report `isBlocked=false`.
-- Current tester delta is limited to `LOGBOOK.md`, `scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh`, and `task-board.config.json`. No product source changed.
-
-## Reproduced gates
-
-| Gate | Result |
-| --- | --- |
-| Configured completion: worktree-safe `make credential-free-validate` | Exit `0`; relay packaging, exact workspace graph, deterministic generation, unsigned macOS host/provider builds and target tests, Core boundaries, full Swift tests, release build, native packaging, legacy preservation, migration isolation negatives, and legacy build/tests passed. |
-| Focused Shared Runtime suites | Eight suites, 105 tests, every suite exit `0`: message codecs, coordinator, provider adapter, VPN session controller, M1 composition, exact macOS ownership, runtime diagnostics, and SSH error mapping. |
-| M1 harness | Six production-entry tests and all seven deterministic fixture rows passed; repeated privacy run exit `0`. |
-| M0 binding/adapter gate | Production permission recomputed `true`; all 32 missing, malformed-as-unknown, narrowed, forged/rebound, dependency-closure, HEV, libssh2, header, patch, and licence negative tests passed. |
-| Platform adapters | `ReluxTunnelIOSAdapter` and `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter` target builds exit `0`. This is compile evidence only and makes no live iOS/provider claim. |
-| Coverage | Full 514-test/44-suite run exit `0`; 25 ReluxNIOSSH rows remain explicit known-unavailable evidence. Selected Shared Runtime/M1 coverage is `4674/5174 = 90.34%` lines and `1620/1921 = 84.33%` regions; package coverage is `92.92%` lines and `85.22%` regions. |
-| Lint/config/diff | Swift format lint, shell syntax, JSON parse, `git diff --check`, and focused credential contract test all exit `0`. |
-| Documentation and diagrams | 52 local links across five relevant documents resolve; PlantUML syntax/render exit `0`; all four rendered SVG pages are byte-identical to checked-in artefacts. |
-| Board | `task-board validate` reports `Board is valid. No issues found.` with exit `0`. |
-
-## Negative evidence and corrections
-
-1. The first configured run exited `2` because the legacy checkout default resolved inside the managed `.temp` worktree. The configured command now derives the control repository from Git's absolute common directory and still fails closed when the checkout is absent.
-2. The next configured run reached `validation-contract-tests` and exited nonzero because its “valid” scheme fixture omitted the two UI-test schemes already required by the production exact-set gate. The fixture and all isolated negative rows now use the complete active graph.
-3. Production call site: `scripts/check-workspace-schemes.sh`, invoked by `scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh` and the deterministic workspace validation. Narrowing only `ReluxProxyIOSUITests` from the production expected set made the named contract test exit `1`; byte-identical restoration (`cmp=0`) returned the focused test and full configured suite to exit `0`. The gate was narrowed, not deleted.
-4. M0 and M1 production-entry tests independently distinguish absent evidence from unreadable/malformed evidence and reject narrower or caller-minted claims; their focused runs passed.
-
-## Provider and system-mutation boundary
-
-- `App/ReluxProxyMacTunnel/Sources/PacketTunnelProvider.swift` was read successfully; a `MacOSProviderCompositionRoot` search returned the expected absence code `1`, while the lifecycle-shell completion path is present. `docs/m1-runtime-ownership-and-operations.md` states the same limitation. No live-provider-wiring claim is made.
-- NetworkExtension configuration and DNS hashes matched before and after the full validation window; the Relux product/harness process count was zero at both endpoints.
-- Broad route-table hashes changed during long builds and are explicitly inconclusive because dynamic host/link routes churn independently. A bounded route-socket monitor around a fresh production-entry harness run recorded 35 `RTM_MISS` lookup events and **zero** `RTM_ADD`, `RTM_DELETE`, `RTM_CHANGE`, `RTM_NEWADDR`, or `RTM_DELADDR` mutation events. Full-tunnel route selectors plus NetworkExtension and DNS hashes matched before/after; harness exit was `0`.
-- Executed paths were source generation, deterministic CLI harnesses, unit/integration tests, compile/build, unsigned Xcode target validation, lint, diagram rendering, board operations, and read-only system observation. No signing, install, NetworkExtension preference write, `startVPNTunnel`, provider launch, route command, DNS write, or physical VPN row ran.
-
-## Fresh evidence files
-
-- `credential-free-validate-04.log`
-- `focused-runtime-02.log`
-- `m1-runtime-harness-02.log`
-- `m0-bindings-02.log`
-- `adapter-builds-02.log`
-- `coverage-report-02.log`
-- `credential-contract-narrowed-mutant-01.log`
-- `lint-01.log`, `final-narrow-validation-01.log`
-- `documentation-integrity-01.log`, `diagram-integrity-01.log`
-- `route-monitor-summary-01.log`, `route-monitor-classification-01.log`
-- `final-candidate-integrity-01.log`, `board-validation-03.log`
-
-No results from the earlier tester run are accepted as substitutes for the gates listed above; every reported pass in this outcome was rerun in the current workspace. The unsigned macOS target evidence is the named `macos-target-builds-and-contracts` step inside `credential-free-validate-04.log` rather than a redundant second Xcode matrix run.
